  body: "# Temporary absence and continued family household membership\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured guidance allows household membership during some temporary absences and considers intended
    return and expected duration, including the source’s qualified treatment of the 52-week boundary.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe chapter concerns JSA(IB) and IS. A shared address, hospital stay
    or fixed number of weeks alone does not determine membership. The source’s intention, previous membership,
    duration and exception wording must remain together; no present-day family or residence finding is
    made.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 22001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda59bc86650c4ab7bb11ee/dmgch22.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 22: Membership of the family.\n- [DMG 22041, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda59bc86650c4ab7bb11ee/dmgch22.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 22: Membership of the family.\n- [DMG 22042, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda59bc86650c4ab7bb11ee/dmgch22.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 22: Membership of the family.\n- [DMG 22043, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5eda59bc86650c4ab7bb11ee/dmgch22.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 22: Membership of the family.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch22`: PDF SHA-256 `f8545cc90dbcffa59e0255fcf5a9335d94c0e29ee7e8a714385a146121959c0d`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `336e01c44bf057e8c30ad34752a8ea72e08961d201c6f61c71a3b897890d2c1e`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-hospital-family-membership
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The general household provision allows temporary absence, supplying the chapter 22
      research context for the hospital family-membership question without treating admission as an
      automatic loss.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch22/0015
      quote: "22041   The claimant’s household may include\n\n        1.     the claimant\n\n        2.\
        \     the claimant’s partner or partners\n\n        3.     the members of a joint-claim couple\n\
        \n        4.     any child or young person who is the responsibility of anyone in 1. or 2.\n\n\
        \        This applies even if any of these people are temporarily living away from the other\n\
        \        members of the family1, for example to work or visit relatives.\n\n        Note: The
        definition of a claimant for JSA(IB) in DMG 22002\n                                          \
        \                         1 JSA Regs, reg 78(1), (1A); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 16(1)\n\n\n\n      \
        \  When can they not be treated as members of the\n        claimant’s household"
      locator: DMG 22041
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch22/0015
      quote: "22043   The absent member may be treated as a member of the claimant’s household if\n\n\
        \        1.     that person intends to resume living with the family and\n\n        2.     the
        absence is unlikely to last\n\n               2.1      more than 52 weeks or\n\n             \
        \  2.2      substantially more than 52 weeks1 where exceptional circumstances\n              \
        \          apply.\n\n        Substantially is not defined in legislation and should be given its
        everyday meaning,\n        that is, in this context - of large size or amount.\n\n        Note:
        This exception only applies if the family has previously lived as members of\n        the same
        household, (notwithstanding that that household may have been abroad)\n        and the intention
        to resume living with the family must not be conditional.\n                                  \
        \                                 1 JSA Regs, reg 78(2)(b); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 16(2)(b)\n\n\n\n\
        \nVol 4 Amendment 32 October 2010"
      locator: DMG 22043
